# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `npm run dev` starts a local Postgres 18 cluster on this URL automatically,
# so you can leave it unset for local development. In production, point it at
# any Postgres (Neon, Supabase, RDS…). On serverless hosts use the provider's
# POOLED connection string (Neon "-pooler" host, Supabase port 6543).
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://dreamtutors:dreamtutors@127.0.0.1:54331/dreamtutors
# DATABASE_SSL_STRICT=true        # once you've confirmed your provider's CA verifies

# ── File storage ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uploaded files are written to this folder on the server's disk.
# LOCAL_UPLOAD_DIR=.uploads

# ── Local-only settings (never set these in production) ───────────────────
# DT_ALLOW_REMOTE_RESET=true     # lets db:reset wipe a non-local DB
# DT_PG_PORT=54331               # port for the embedded local cluster
# ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS=192.168.1.70  # dev server: allow phones on your LAN (Expo shell)
